=== PE 881: Divisor Graph Width ===

The width of a divisor lattice for N = ∏ p_i^{e_i}
is the maximum coefficient in ∏ (1 + x + ... + x^{e_i}).

=== Widths for powers of primorials ===
  primorial_1 = 2: width = 1
  primorial_2 = 6: width = 2
  primorial_3 = 30: width = 3
  primorial_4 = 210: width = 6
  primorial_5 = 2310: width = 10
  primorial_6 = 30030: width = 20

=== N=60 variants (same prime set, different exponents) ===
  N=  60: width=4
  N=  72: width=3
  N=  90: width=4
  N= 120: width=4
  N= 180: width=5
  N= 360: width=6

PE answer: 205702861096933200
